#X obj 60 608 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 636 1 float: note number. Velocity is taken from inlet 2 \;   and velocity 0 is a note off. \; 1 list: note \, velocity and \, if you like \, the MIDI channel. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages. \; 2 float: velocity for the next note \, 0 to 127 (default 100). \; 3 float or list: raw MIDI bytes \, as midiin gives them. \; 3 anything: a message \, the same set as inlet 1., f 64;
#X obj 60 762 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 790 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: info \, name \, 0-127 and value text for every \;   change \, the patch that plays \, its names \, the channels. \; 3 float: SysEx bytes for midiout., f 64;
#X obj 60 884 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 912 name v: set a control \, in the values the D-50 shows. \; name: report it as info. \; n name v: set it from a pot or a MIDI CC \, 0 to 127. \; ninfo name: report it as info. \; preset n: a factory preset \, read only. \; user n: a slot of the user bank \, 0 to 63. \; init: a plain sawtooth patch to start from. \; reload: the same patch again \, edits dropped. \; store n: the playing patch into user slot n \, in memory. \; userwrite: write the user bank to d50user-bank.syx. \; userread: read it again. Both also take a file name. \; usersend: the user bank as SysEx on outlet 3. \; presets \, users: list the names. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bendrange. \; mod f: modulation lever \, 0 to 1. \; aftertouch f: channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; channel n: MIDI receive channel \, 0 is all. \; txchannel n: channel of the controller feedback and device \;   number of SysEx dumps \, 1 to 16. \; status: report patch \, names \, channels \, voices and CPU. \; stop: all notes off. \; reset: all notes off and the effect tails emptied., f 64;
#X obj 60 1294 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1322 midiin: raw bytes into inlet 3. d50~ takes notes \, bend \, \;   aftertouch \, program change \, CC 1 (lever) \, 5 (portamento \;   time) \, 7 (volume) \, 64 (hold) \, 65 (portamento) and SysEx. \; midiout: the floats of outlet 3 \, SysEx answers and dumps. \; d50cc 1: the CC pages 20 to 119 on channel 1. \; d50pads 10 \, lkdisplay: the Launchkey (see Launchkey). \; channel 1 at load: d50~ plays channel 1 only \, so the pads \;   on channel 10 do not play notes. \; Without midiin: send note lists and bend \, mod \, sustain., f 64;
#X obj 60 1480 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1508 cut (0): cutoff of every synth partial \, also of notes that are sounding. 0 leaves the patch as it is. \; res (0): resonance of every synth partial \, for the notes that follow. \; att (0): attack (TVA time 1) of all four partials \, for the notes that follow. \; rel (0): release (TVA and TVF time 5) of all four partials \, for the notes that follow. \; chorus (patch): chorus balance of both tones. \; reverb (patch): reverb balance of the patch. \; balance (patch): balance of the two tones \, lower at 0 \, upper at 100. \; volume (80): master volume \, not stored in a patch., f 64;
#X obj 60 1730 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controller\ layer\ and\ editor 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1758 d50cc is the controller layer: MIDI CC 20 to 119 in pages of 8 \, the same pages as for pdoly8~ and tx81z~. Page 1 is the performance row \, page k is row k of the editor. It turns a CC into an n message and sends every change made elsewhere back to the controller as CC. Its argument is the MIDI channel \, and it follows the channels d50~ reports. \; d50edit is the editor: click it in the object area above. All 117 controls in rows of 8 \, the factory presets and the user bank \, the MIDI channels and SysEx. It explains itself in its readme. \; The D-50 has four partials \, two per tone. A partial name such as cutoff acts on the selected partial \, a tone name such as structure on the tone it belongs to. part 0 to 3 selects U1 \, U2 \, L1 \, L2. All names are listed at the end of this patch with their CC numbers., f 64;
#X obj 60 2012 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Launchkey 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2040 Launchkey: the Novation Launchkey Mini MK4 with the custom firmware maltepeter2000/launchkey_firmware \, set up the same for every instrument of bela-workstation (launchkey/README.md there). \; d50cc 1: the controller layer. Encoders in mode Custom 1 send CC pages from 20 in rows of 8 on the keys channel \, every change made elsewhere goes back to them on the send channel (txchannel of d50~) \, CC 3 asks for all values. \; d50pads 10: the pads in Drum mode (notes 36-51 on channel 10 \, the Drums Channel): top row 36 factory + \, 37 user + \, 38 init (press twice within a second) \, 39-43 own \, bottom row 44 factory - \, 45 user - \, 46 save \, 47-51 own. d50~ has no own pads yet. \; Pad colours \, sent by d50pads itself with noteout on channel 10 (velocity = colour + 32 x mode): factory blue \, user green \, init orange (flashing while the second press is awaited) \, save red (white for a moment when pressed) \, own pads purple \, free pads off. They go out at load \, on leds \, and when the Launchkey asks for them (CC 3 = 127 on channel 10 \, sent when Drum mode is selected). \; lkdisplay: the display lines (display <title> <value>: the control you turn \, Preset \, User \, Init or Stored with the patch name) as SysEx for the Launchkey's display -> midiout., f 64;
#X obj 60 2422 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2450 The object contains no Roland data. It loads its files from the folder of the external \, or else from the folder of the patch. \; d50_pcm.bin: the PCM samples \, written by tools/make_d50_data.py from your own ROM images. Without it the object stays silent and says so in the Pd window. \; Every .syx file beside it is read as a factory bank \, a D-50 bulk dump of 64 patches. The files are loaded in alphabetical order \, PND50-00.syx first \, and their patches are numbered through. Without one the object plays eight built-in presets \, which cannot be edited. \; d50user-bank.syx: the user bank \, in the same format. Until it has been written the user bank holds 64 init patches. \; A D-50 dump ends with the data of its reverb types 17 to 32. The object does not use them \, its reverbs are built in \, but it keeps the block of the dump it came with and puts it into every bank it writes or sends \, so a D-50 gets a complete dump back. \; The engine runs at 32 kHz \, the rate of the original \, and is resampled to the rate of Pd., f 64;
#X obj 60 2784 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 2836 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2812 4 0 127 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2836 preset \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2812 4 0 63 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2836 user \$1;
#X obj 60 2872 r \$0-d50-out;
#X obj 60 2896 route preset user;
#X obj 60 2922 unpack f s;
#X floatatom 60 2950 4 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X symbolatom 100 2950 20 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 260 2922 unpack f s;
#X floatatom 260 2950 4 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X symbolatom 300 2950 20 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 82 2978 preset selects a factory preset \, user a slot of the user bank. The third outlet answers with the number and the name. \; A patch change sets the first four controls of the performance row (cut \, res \, att \, rel) back to 0. \; store 5 followed by userwrite keeps the playing patch in user slot 5 and on disk. The editor does both with save patch., f 64;
#X obj 60 3088 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Patch\ editing 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3116 A few examples \, the editor has them all. Values are the ones the D-50 shows \, fine for example runs from -50 to 50. A name without a value reports the current one. \; A partial or tone edit is heard from the next note on. Chorus \, equalizer \, reverb and the balances follow at once \, and cut also moves the notes that are sounding. \; The built-in presets cannot be edited. Load a bank \, or start from init or a user slot., f 64;
#X obj 460 3272 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3248 6 0 3 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3272 part \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3248 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 3272 cutoff \$1;
#X floatatom 260 3248 6 0 30 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 3272 reso \$1;
#X floatatom 360 3248 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 3272 level \$1;
#X text 82 3302 part (0): the partial that cutoff \, reso \, level and the other partial names act on. 0 to 3 are U1 \, U2 \, L1 \, L2. \; cutoff (patch): filter cutoff of the selected partial. Only synth partials have a filter \, a PCM partial ignores it. \; reso (patch): filter resonance. \; level (patch): level of the partial., f 64;
#X obj 460 3426 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3402 6 1 7 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3426 structure \$1;
#X text 82 3456 structure (patch): which partials of the tone are synth or PCM and whether they are ring modulated \, see Tone controls., f 64;
#X obj 460 3516 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 3492 6 0 8 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 3516 keymode \$1;
#X text 82 3546 keymode (patch): whole \, dual \, split and their solo variants \, see Patch controls., f 64;
#X obj 60 3592 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty By\ address 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 3620 s \$0-d50;
#X msg 60 3620 l2 cutoff 30;
#X msg 190 3620 l2 cutoff;
#X msg 320 3620 dump;
#X msg 60 3654 param 13 60;
#X msg 190 3654 param 13;
#X msg 320 3654 sysexdump;
#X text 82 3688 l2 cutoff 30: section \, name and value set a parameter without changing the selection. The sections are u1 \, u2 \, upper \, l1 \, l2 \, lower and patch. Without a value the message reports it. \; dump: reports the three names and every named parameter of every section \, 311 messages. \; param a v: sets one of the 448 bytes of the patch by address \, with the value a D-50 dump stores. The address is the section times 64 plus the offset \, sections counted from 0 in the order above. param a reports the byte. \; name: patch name My Patch sets the patch name \, up to 18 characters. upper name and lower name take up to 10. \; sysexdump: sends the playing patch as SysEx \, see below., f 64;
#X obj 60 3894 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty SysEx 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3922 The object speaks the exclusive format of the D-50 \, so an editor or librarian made for the D-50 can program it \, and it can exchange patches with a real D-50. The bytes arrive with the rest of the MIDI at the third inlet and leave the third outlet as floats. \; Data set (DT1) to address 00-00-00 edits the playing patch \, the same 448 bytes that param reaches. Data set to 02-00-00 \, the internal memory of the D-50 \, goes to the user bank: a bulk dump replaces it in memory \, userwrite keeps it. \; A request (RQ1) for either area is answered at the third outlet. sysexdump sends the playing patch and usersend the user bank without being asked. \; sysex followed by the bytes of one message does the same from a list. The device number of incoming messages is not checked \, answers carry the number of the request., f 64;
#X obj 60 4176 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Playing 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 4228 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 4204 6 -1 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 4228 bend \$1;
#X floatatom 160 4204 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 4228 mod \$1;
#X floatatom 260 4204 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 4228 aftertouch \$1;
#X floatatom 360 4204 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 4228 sustain \$1;
#X text 82 4258 bend (0): pitch wheel \, -1 to 1. The range in semitones is bendrange. \; mod (0): modulation lever \, 0 to 1. What it does is part of the patch. \; aftertouch (0): channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain (0): hold pedal. Notes released while it is 1 sound until it returns to 0., f 64;
#X obj 60 4384 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Additional\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
